    the useVehicles vehicle pick); the view performs NO HTTP.
  Projection -> SleepEfficiencyBuilder is a 1:1 port of the web gauge + stat memos:
    efficiencyColor (>95 good / >85 warning / else critical, STRICT comparisons); gauge value clamped
    0..100; avgDrainPerDay = (sentry_off_drain_rate ?? 0) * 24; totalSleepHours = sum of total_minutes
    over state == "asleep" || "offline", / 60; wakeEventsCount = recent_events.length. Verified by an
    EXECUTED harness (34/34, below) — real cached->projection, not a typecheck.
  Composition -> WidgetShell chrome (moon icon + "Sleep Efficiency" title + "?" help popover + freshness
    chip + refresh) · COMPACT (cols<=1, the default 1x2 footprint): the 70pt dial alone, no dial label,
    no stats (header title/icon/help hidden, matching the web compact branch passing undefined and
    WidgetGaugeHero hiding stats) · STANDARD (cols>=2): the 100pt dial + "Efficiency" label + the three
    GaugeHeroStats ("Avg Drain/Day" {2dp}%, "Total Sleep" {0dp}h, "Wake Events" {count}). web RadialGauge
    SVG arc -> SwiftUI Circle().trim().stroke() rotated -90° (track + tone-colored progress arc + centered
    "{value}%"), Reduce-Motion-aware fill. Recharts/Leaflet -> none. The web decorative Moon lucide icon is
    rendered Apple-idiomatically as the SF Symbol moon.fill (header) / moon.zzz (empty).
  States (all render) -> loading (circular skeleton chrome) · empty ("No sleep efficiency data",
    ContentUnavailableView) · error (retry) · stale (chip + banner over cached data) · offline (cached data
    + chip + banner) · content. Model phase resolution keeps cached data visible behind refresh/errors,
    matching the web shell (skeleton only on initial fetch; empty only when hasData == false, i.e.
    summary == nil).
  i18n -> ALL 7 web source t() keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade with the web t(key,default) fallback:
    widget.sleepEfficiency.{efficiency,avgDrain,totalSleep,hours,wakeEvents,title,noData} -> ALL PRESENT in
    SleepEfficiencyWidget.strings; plus help.sleepEfficiency.body (WidgetShell help). The web's hardcoded
    gauge unit literal '%' is promoted to a catalog key (widget.sleepEfficiency.percent); the registry
